  "reason": "The two completed experiments (config_050: multimodal/weighted, acc=0.520; config_010: RNA-only, acc=0.514) show only a marginal accuracy gain from adding the image modality, while F1 actually drops, suggesting the fusion strategy may be suboptimal. Config_040 is identical to config_050 except it uses concat fusion instead of weighted fusion, providing a clean single-variable ablation. This directly tests whether the weighted fusion is the bottleneck or whether a simple concatenation of modality representations performs comparably or better. Resolving this question early is critical: if concat outperforms weighted, it opens a clear exploitation path across other encoders; if they are similar, the fusion choice is not the limiting factor and I should pivot to testing alternative RNA encoders (pca_n2000, scvi_n200) in the remaining budget. With 7 experiments left, isolating this one variable now maximizes information per experiment."
}

